7:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-slate max-w-none dark:prose-invert prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:tracking-tight prose-p:leading-8 prose-a:text-blue-700","children":[["$","section","Workflow 1: assemble a clean PDF packet",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Workflow 1: assemble a clean PDF packet"}],[["$","p","Before merging PDFs, open each source file and confirm it belongs in the packet. Rename files in the intended order, remove duplicates, and check page orientation. A merge tool can combine files quickly, but it cannot decide whether an appendix should appear before a signature page.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Before merging PDFs, open each source file and confirm it belongs in the packet. Rename files in the intended order, remove duplicates, and check page orientation. A merge tool can combine files quickly, but it cannot decide whether an appendix should appear before a signature page."}]]}],["$","p","After merging, open the output and verify page count, reading order, and visual quality. This final check is especially important for contracts, invoices, client reports, and school submissions where a missing page creates follow-up work.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"After merging, open the output and verify page count, reading order, and visual quality. This final check is especially important for contracts, invoices, client reports, and school submissions where a missing page creates follow-up work."}]]}]]]}],["$","section","Workflow 2: extract only the useful pages",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Workflow 2: extract only the useful pages"}],[["$","p","Splitting is often better than sending a full PDF. If a recipient needs pages 3-5 from a 40-page report, extract those pages and share a smaller, clearer document. The result is easier to read, easier to attach, and less likely to expose unrelated information.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Splitting is often better than sending a full PDF. If a recipient needs pages 3-5 from a 40-page report, extract those pages and share a smaller, clearer document. The result is easier to read, easier to attach, and less likely to expose unrelated information."}]]}],["$","p","Keep the source file unchanged and export a new file for the extracted pages. Use clear filenames that include the page range or purpose so recipients understand what they received.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Keep the source file unchanged and export a new file for the extracted pages. Use clear filenames that include the page range or purpose so recipients understand what they received."}]]}]]]}],["$","section","Workflow 3: move between PDFs and images",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Workflow 3: move between PDFs and images"}],[["$","p","PDF-to-image conversion is useful for support articles, design reviews, thumbnails, and documentation. Choose a resolution that matches the target use: smaller for web previews, larger for print or detailed review.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"PDF-to-image conversion is useful for support articles, design reviews, thumbnails, and documentation. Choose a resolution that matches the target use: smaller for web previews, larger for print or detailed review."}]]}],["$","p","Image-to-PDF is useful when scans, receipts, whiteboard photos, or screenshots need to become a single shareable document. Put images in the right order before exporting, and check the final PDF on both desktop and mobile viewers.",{"children":["$Lf"]}]]]}],"$L10"]}]
